From 70e97ec3cf466840c69a9631c8129cf0823b6d0f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AEON-7 <aeon-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 20:09:33 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [ROCm][Inkling2] AEON per-request multi-variant o_proj
 ablation

Original AEON work. Off (zero cost) unless AEON_VARIANT_DIR is set.

One server holds a bank of registered ablation variants and applies the
right one to every token of every request in a mixed batch, so an
abliteration screen runs many edits concurrently with no restart.

- aeon_variants.py: variant files (dirs [D] / [24,D] / [48,D] / [48,K,D],
  scales [48] / [48,K]), worker-side bank with slot table, per-step
  per-token variant map built from the batch request order, and a fused
  Triton kernel after wo_ud that applies y <- y - s r (r . y) for K
  directions in fp32 per row, in place. Stock rows are never touched; no
  launch when no request in the step uses a variant.
- model_runner: record each request variant on add, build the token map
  after prepare_attn. Refuses cudagraph modes (eager only for now).
- OpenAI chat/completions: "aeon_variant" field (or vllm_xargs), checked
  against the registry (400 if unknown) and folded into the prefix-cache
  salt so KV is never shared across variants.
- HTTP: GET/POST /aeon/variants, DELETE /aeon/variants/{name}.

Signed-off-by: AEON-7 <aeon-7@users.noreply.github.com>
